# Fixture: current_section is one pointer for the WHOLE walk, never reset
# on entering/leaving an included file (walker.py's own _walk_nodes
# comment calls this out; unexercised anywhere in starter/configs). This
# is a case a reimplementation would "correct" by accident if it scoped
# current_section per file, e.g. as a stack pushed/popped around
# _enter_file.
#
# @include must appear before any section header in the file it's written
# in (parser.py's own rule) — so this file never sets a section of its
# own at all. included.pfcfg ends on a bare [x] section header with
# nothing under it in that file. The very next node here, after the
# include returns, is a bare assignment with no section header anywhere
# in THIS file — it must land under [x] (included.pfcfg's last section),
# not raise "no section ever set".
@include included.pfcfg

after = also-lands-under-x
